<p>Britain’s Green Party won the parliamentary by-election in Gorton and Denton, near Manchester, electing local councillor Hannah Spencer and taking a seat Labour had held for almost a century. Several outlets called it the Greens’ first-ever win in a British parliamentary by-election—a milestone that points to more voters looking beyond the two main parties. The result drew national attention for another reason: Prime Minister Keir Starmer’s governing Labour Party slipped into third place, adding to questions about his leadership and strategy after weeks of turbulence and internal pressure. Reform UK came second, a reminder that competition on both the left and right is reshaping the political map in places that used to look secure. For many voters, the campaign focused on cost-of-living pressures. Spencer ran on an anti-inequality message, while Green leader Zack Polanski pushed for a bigger national-media presence alongside local organizing—an approach the party says can turn grassroots energy into electoral breakthroughs.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Ba_p4h1rEJp0DrfFPBvJaS5RlMAL8RWb7eKg6Fk_9FumXqB6307D0J9bgYhmhf2oJf3cfdcapczk1J_W60P4fmWy0LoRn8bnBUxU4O0qjtjFCoEMpCYajTuPRVw49t62Wmw-5Xnf1T5PG8A0tMsgPJYVLJ2esdE3IEVaFWD_VHs0MD0H5xSwj9c_CAJQxGGSviWfq75unKg' alt='Hannah Spencer, the Green Party’s by-election winner, outside a polling station in Gorton and Denton near Manchester.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Vote breakdown: Spencer won with 14,980 votes (40.6%), ahead of Reform UK’s Matt Goodwin on 10,578 (28.7%) and Labour’s Angeliki Stogia on 9,364 (25.4%), with a 4,402 majority reported by POLITICO.</li><li>Big swings: POLITICO said the Green vote share rose 27.4 percentage points versus 2024, Reform’s rose 14.6 points, and Labour’s fell 25.4 points.</li><li>Campaign narrative: POLITICO described Polanski as borrowing Nigel Farage’s media playbook by putting himself front and center. The Greens also faced accusations of “stoking division”; Polanski told POLITICO, “I don’t want everyone to agree with what I or the Green Party is saying”.</li><li>Pre-vote polling: Ahead of the vote, The Hindu reported local voting-intention figures of Labour 28%, Greens 28% and Reform UK 27%, pointing to a tight three-way squeeze.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Green Party (Zack Polanski): Polanski said the Greens are best placed to beat Reform UK after the result, according to the Guardian’s live coverage. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/feb/27/gorton-and-denton-byelection-result-labour-green-party-reform-uk-politics-latest-news'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Green Party (party source): A Green Party source told the Press Association the result felt like a “seismic moment” and said, “Greens are here to stay now as a progressive voice in British politics”. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/feb/27/gorton-and-denton-byelection-result-labour-green-party-reform-uk-politics-latest-news'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Novara Media (commentary panel): Novara Media framed the by-election as potentially decisive for Starmer’s future, and its program description discussed allegations of Labour “dirty tricks” and campaign smears. (<a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/02/26/the-by-election-that-could-end-starmer/'>Novara Media</a>)</li><li>New York Times (analysis): The New York Times said the outcome signaled frustration among left-leaning voters with Starmer’s government. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/26/world/europe/gorton-denton-result-green-party-labour.html'>New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3344829/starmer-reels-greens-seize-labour-stronghold-uk-special-election'>Starmer reels as Greens seize Labour stronghold in UK special election</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/uk-pms-labour-party-loses-greater-manchester-seat-it-held-it-for-a-century-green-partys-hannah-spencer-wins-gorton-denton-11143446#publisher=newsstand'>UK PM&#x27;s Labour Party Loses Greater Manchester Seat. It Held It For A Century</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/26/world/europe/gorton-denton-result-green-party-labour.html'>Green Party Defeats Labour in U.K. Special Election, in Blow to Starmer</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/02/26/the-by-election-that-could-end-starmer/'>The By-Election That Could End Starmer</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/embarrassing-defeat-for-uks-starmer-as-greens-seize-labour-stronghold'>Embarrassing defeat for British PM Starmer as Greens seize Labour stronghold</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/c7fee9cc-2bb1-457d-a94c-f60bc30da018'>Greens win key UK by-election in blow to Labour</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/voters-go-to-polls-in-crucial-bye-election-test-for-uks-starmer/article70680369.ece'>Voters go to polls in crucial bye-election test for U.K.’s Starmer</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/britains-green-party-wins-special-election-seat-parliament-130553562'>Britain’s Green Party wins a special election for a seat in Parliament</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/zack-polanski-populist-pitch-pays-off-in-gorton-denton-by-election-united-kingdom-hannah-spencer/'>Zack Polanski’s populist pitch pays off in Gorton and Denton</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/feb/27/gorton-and-denton-byelection-result-labour-green-party-reform-uk-politics-latest-news'>Polanski says Greens best party to defeat Reform after Spencer wins Gorton and Denton – UK politics live</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>